Z||000000||Axmanmkii||12-27-2001||10:47 PM||||Hey guys, I'm making plans on getting a 'new' car. Currently I own a Eclipse GS, and I want to keep it cause I put too much work into it.<P>So I'm thinking about getting a real 'sport' car. I use the word sport loosely cause basicly I'm looking for anything with modding potential.<P>So currently I'm thinking about getting a:<P>1. SHO- A decent sport sedan with a awesome masterpiece of a engine<P>and just recently<P>2. Fiero- The first and only American made Mid(rear?)-placment car.<P>Did a few quick search on both cars. I can find Fiero easier, but they're more expensive compare to a 1G SHO. The average price to a use Fiero is under $3000, while the SHO is under $2000.<P>But is there anything I should know about the Fiero? My mom said my cousin, Cindy, had a GT ATX, that she later fried the tranny by trying to hual 8 people in it. I dont really care about ATXs, since I perfer to drive a stick. But are all the trannies weak?<P>Also, what is it auto-x potential? Drag racing potential? Daily Driven potential? <P>And is there any good information websites about these cars? <P>Well, hopefully these are great reliable cars that will last a century one stock parts.I doupt that somehow....<P>But thanks all!||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroHarry||12-27-2001||11:04 PM||||Hey man,<P>Use the search option in the upper corner to find all the needed info you could ever want to hear!<P>Personally I would go Fiero, but im very biased <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Much more potentail for upgrades and racing possibilitys!<P>------------------<BR><BR><B>"If you want to blend in, take the bus!"</B>||||reg||1
Z||000002||stimpy||12-27-2001||11:23 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Axmanmkii:<BR>[B]My mom said my cousin, Cindy, had a GT ATX, that she later fried the tranny by trying to hual 8 people in it. /B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Huh?! I suspect if your cuz was the type of freewheelin gal that would try to fit 8 people in the Fiero, then there were probably bigger issues there than the tranny being a "weak design". The transaxles in Fieros are the same that were put in many fwd GM cars of that era, including station wagons like the Celebrity and Pontiac 6000, so I don't think the load was any issue at all.<P>Anyhow, welcome to the forum. The Fiero definately has mucho modding potential. I like the SHO too, either car would be a good pick to plaster a smile on your face, although they represent very different segments of the market. Have fun picking one out. <P>------------------<BR>Loud Pipes Save Lives!             <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/stimpy_sig.gif">       <BR>My Fiero website-&gt; <A HREF="http://www.dancinghamsters.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.dancinghamsters.com/</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||GTFiero1||12-27-2001||11:48 PM||||here ya go: <A HREF="http://www.v8archie.com" TARGET=_blank>www.v8archie.com</A>   if fiero trans axles can hold up under the raw torque of a chevy V-8 than obviously your sister had something wrong with hers ( maybe negelected to check the tanny fluid)<P>------------------<BR>Adam J. B.<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fiero_3.jpg">   <BR>you gotta keep on keepin on...<BR>IM AOL: GTFiero &  Rumpdetective (dont ask)||||reg||1
Z||000004||frontal lobe||12-28-2001||02:16 AM||||I've heard of people on the forum auto-crossing and drag-racing them, but my experience is as a daily driver.<P>I have a v-6 5-speed that is very smooth with lots of low end torque.  I get 25 mpg in the city and about 30 hwy.<P>SHO would be fun, but like Stimpy says, a different kind of car.  Everything I've read about them shows a poor repair record, but that is heresay.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Indy-2M4||12-28-2001||05:52 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Axmanmkii:<BR><B> My mom said my cousin, Cindy, had a GT ATX, that she later fried the tranny by trying to hual 8 people in it. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Welcome to the forum, but may I ask  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif"> how in the heck did she manage to get 8 people in a Fiero??!! I am assuming the car had T-tops or a sunroof? Even then!<P><BR>------------------<BR>Kathy<BR>http:\\sofa.iwarp.com<BR>    <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/IndyCrueSig.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by Indy-2M4 (edited 12-28-2001).]||||reg||1
